DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     rrddiisstt is a program to maintain identical copies of files over multiple
     hosts.  It preserves the owner, group, mode, and mtime of files if possi‐
     ble and can update programs that are executing.

     rrddiisstt reads commands from _d_i_s_t_f_i_l_e to direct the updating of files and/or
     directories.  If _d_i_s_t_f_i_l_e is ‘-’, the standard input is used.  If no --ff
     option is present, the program looks first for _d_i_s_t_f_i_l_e, then _D_i_s_t_f_i_l_e,
     to use as the input.  If no names are specified on the command line,
     rrddiisstt will update all of the files and directories listed in _d_i_s_t_f_i_l_e.
     If the file _/_e_t_c_/_D_i_s_t_f_i_l_e exists, it will be run automatically by the
     clock daemon cron(8), via the system script daily(8).

     If _n_a_m_e is specified, it is taken to be the name of a file to be updated
     or the label of a command to execute.  If label and file names conflict,
     it is assumed to be a label.  These may be used together to update spe‐
     cific files using specific commands.

     rrddiisstt uses a remote shell command to access each target host.  By de‐
     fault, ssh(1) is used unless overridden by the --PP option or the RSH envi‐
     ronment variable.  If the target host is the string “localhost” and the
     remote user name is the same as the local user name, rrddiisstt will run the
     command:

           /bin/sh -c rdistd -S

     Otherwise, rrddiisstt will run the command:

           ssh <host> -l <login_name> rdistd -S

     _h_o_s_t is the name of the target host; _l_o_g_i_n___n_a_m_e is the name of the user
     to make the connection as.

     On each target host rrddiisstt will attempt to run the command:

           rdistd -S

     Or if the --pp option was specified, rrddiisstt will attempt to run the command:

           <rdistd path> -S

     If no --pp option is specified, or ⟨_r_d_i_s_t_d _p_a_t_h⟩ is a simple filename,
     rdistd(1) or ⟨_r_d_i_s_t_d _p_a_t_h⟩ must be somewhere in the PATH of the user run‐
     ning rrddiisstt on the remote (target) host.

